# FPGA 8-bit Console Project Structure

The project is organized into several key directories:

## RTL Source Files
The [rtl/](mdc:rtl) directory contains all hardware description files:
- SystemVerilog modules in `.sv` files
- Legacy Verilog modules in `.v` files
- Memory initialization files in `.hex` format

Key files:
- [rtl/top.sv](mdc:rtl/top.sv): Top-level module for FPGA synthesis
- @rtl/top_simulator.sv: Top-level module for simulation (i.e. `make run`)
- [rtl/chip.sv](mdc:rtl/chip.sv): Main chip implementation
- [rtl/cpu6502_arlet.sv](mdc:rtl/cpu6502_arlet.sv): 6502 CPU implementation
- [rtl/clocks.sv](mdc:rtl/clocks.sv): Clock generation and reset handling
- [rtl/por.sv](mdc:rtl/por.sv): Power-on reset controller
- [rtl/ram_async.sv](mdc:rtl/ram_async.sv): Asynchronous RAM implementation
- [rtl/addressdecoder.sv](mdc:rtl/addressdecoder.sv): Memory address decoding

## Assembly Source
The [src/](mdc:src) directory contains 6502 assembly code:
- [src/main.asm](mdc:src/main.asm): Main program
- [src/memory.cfg](mdc:src/memory.cfg): Memory layout configuration

## Simulation Environment
The [rust/](mdc:rust) directory contains the Verilator-based simulation:
- [rust/src/main.rs](mdc:rust/src/main.rs): Simulation entry point
- [rust/build.rs](mdc:rust/build.rs): Verilator build configuration

## Build System
- [Makefile](mdc:Makefile): Main build automation
- Assembly build: `make asm` to compile assembly code
- Simulation: `make run` to build and run simulator
